@startuml
title preview-hub v1 — Create environment (phub up)

actor "User / PR bot" as Caller
participant "CLI (inside phub-hub container)" as CLI
participant "CreateEnvironment" as UC
participant "EnvLock\n(/state/locks/<env>.lock on volume phub-state)" as Lock
database "Registry (SQLite)" as DB
participant "GitSource" as Git
participant "PlanBuilder" as Plan
participant "Runner (ComposeRunner)" as Run
participant "Docker (Colima preview-hub)" as Docker

Caller -> CLI: up --name feat-x --set backend=feat-x [--ttl 24h]
CLI -> UC: execute(spec)
UC -> Lock: acquire exclusive (non-blocking; busy -> "operation in progress")
group SQLite txn 1 (BEGIN IMMEDIATE)
  UC -> DB: find active env by name
  alt exists and same requested refs and READY
    UC --> CLI: current status (idempotent no-op)
  else exists and different refs
    UC --> CLI: reject: use `phub update` (explicit)
  else not exists
    UC -> DB: insert environments(state=REQUESTED, spec after catalog defaults)\ninsert operations(CREATE, RUNNING, pid, heartbeat)
  end
end
UC -> Git: resolve(repo, ref) for every service (ls-remote)
group SQLite txn 2
  UC -> DB: state=RESOLVING -> BUILDING; insert environment_services(commit_sha, image)
end
UC -> Git: checkout(repo, sha) into /src/<service>/<sha> on volume phub-src (shared, read-only)
UC -> Plan: build(env, manifests, catalog) -> EnvironmentPlan\n(requires order, injected env, routes, labels, resources)
UC -> Run: build images missing for (service, sha) — skip if image exists
note right: build concurrency <= 2 (hub-wide semaphore);\nheartbeat updated between steps
group SQLite txn 3
  UC -> DB: state=STARTING
end
UC -> Run: apply(plan): compose up -d project phub-feat-x\n(network phub-feat-x, volumes phub-feat-x-*, labels dev.phub.env=feat-x)
Run -> Docker: create/start db -> migrate/seed job -> services
Run -> Docker: connect phub-proxy to network phub-feat-x (routes by labels)
UC -> Run: health(env) until all HEALTHY or timeout
alt all healthy
  group SQLite txn 4
    UC -> DB: state=READY, public_url/health per service; op SUCCEEDED
  end
else failure at any step after insert
  group SQLite txn 4'
    UC -> DB: state=FAILED, last_error(stage, service, log excerpt); op FAILED
  end
  note right: objects are left for inspection;\n`phub down` removes them by label
end
UC -> Lock: release
UC --> CLI: status + URLs + pinned commits

newpage preview-hub v1 — Delete environment (phub down) and TTL expiry

actor "User / bot / expiry sweep" as Caller
participant "DeleteEnvironment" as UC
participant "EnvLock" as Lock
database "Registry (SQLite)" as DB
participant "Runner" as Run
participant "Docker" as Docker

Caller -> UC: execute(name)
UC -> Lock: acquire exclusive
group SQLite txn 1
  UC -> DB: find env by name (any state)
  alt none or DELETED
    UC -> Run: inventory(label dev.phub.env=name)
    note right: still sweep stray labelled objects
  else active
    UC -> DB: state=DELETING; insert operations(DELETE, RUNNING)
  end
end
UC -> Run: destroy(env) = compose down -v for project\n+ remove any object with label dev.phub.env=name\n+ disconnect proxy from network
Run -> Docker: remove containers, networks, volumes (label-scoped only)
UC -> Run: inventory(label) must be empty
alt empty
  group SQLite txn 2
    UC -> DB: state=DELETED, deleted_at; op SUCCEEDED
  end
else leftovers
  group SQLite txn 2'
    UC -> DB: state stays DELETING, op FAILED with leftover list
  end
end
UC -> Lock: release

note over Caller, Docker
  ExpireEnvironments (every 15 min by the phub-hub container's own gc loop, or `phub gc`):
  select READY|FAILED where ttl_expires_at < now -> DeleteEnvironment per env (skip if lock busy).
  Stale RUNNING operation (pid gone, heartbeat older than 10 min) -> INTERRUPTED, env -> FAILED.
end note

newpage preview-hub v1 — PR comment bot (phub-bot, revision 3)

participant "phub-bot (poll loop)" as Bot
participant "GitHubApi" as GH
database "Registry (SQLite, bot tables)" as DB
participant "phub-hub (docker exec phub ...)" as Hub

loop every 20 s, per catalog repository
  Bot -> GH: GET issues/comments?since=<cursor - 60 s>
  loop each comment on a PR starting with /preview
    group SQLite txn
      Bot -> DB: INSERT bot_comments(comment_id, ..., RECEIVED)
      note right: primary-key conflict = already handled -> skip
    end
    Bot -> GH: GET pull (head.repo, head.sha, base.repo, state)
    alt author not OWNER/MEMBER/COLLABORATOR, fork PR, closed PR, or parse error
      Bot -> DB: status=REJECTED, error
      Bot -> GH: POST reply (reason)
    else authorized
      Bot -> DB: status=RUNNING, environment=pr-<service>-<number>
      Bot -> Hub: phub up|update|status|down <env> --set <service>=<head.sha> [other svc=ref] --format json
      Hub --> Bot: result JSON / exit code
      Bot -> DB: status=DONE|FAILED
      Bot -> GH: POST single reply (state, URLs, pinned commits or failure stage)
      Bot -> DB: reply_comment_id
    end
  end
  Bot -> DB: advance cursor to newest comment updated_at
  Bot -> GH: GET pulls?state=closed&sort=updated since closed_checked_at
  Bot -> Hub: phub down pr-<service>-<number> for each closed PR with an environment
end
note over Bot, Hub
  A crash between RUNNING and DONE: on restart, RUNNING rows older than 10 min are marked FAILED and
  get a reply "interrupted, run the command again"; the hub's own stale-operation recovery handles the environment.
  Reply posting failures are retried on the next loop while reply_comment_id is NULL (at most 3 attempts).
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title Revision 4 — Create an environment from the dashboard (public)

actor "Owner (browser)" as User
participant "Cloudflare edge\n(Access, free)" as CF
participant "phub-cloudflared\n(VM, outbound tunnel)" as Tun
participant "phub-hub HTTP (C9)" as Web
participant "AccessVerifier\n(JWKS cache)" as Auth
participant "GitHubClient\n(token file, read)" as GH
participant "phub up (child process, C5)" as CLI
database "Registry (SQLite)" as DB

User -> CF: https://preview-hub.cafitac.com
CF -> User: Access login (email OTP) if no session
CF -> Tun: request + Cf-Access-Jwt-Assertion
Tun -> Web: GET /api/catalog
Web -> Auth: verify(jwt) (RS256, aud, iss, exp)
alt invalid / missing / config missing
  Web --> User: 403 (fail closed)
end
Web -> GH: list branches + open PRs per catalog repo (60 s cache)
Web --> User: choices (main / branch / PR #n)
User -> Web: POST /api/environments {services: {backend: "pr-4", frontend: "main"}}
Web -> Auth: verify(jwt); check Origin == dashboard host
Web -> CLI: spawn phub up c-x7k2qa --set backend=pr-4 --set frontend=main\n(requested_by web:<email>)
CLI -> GH: GET pulls/4 -> open, same repo -> head.sha
CLI -> DB: same create flow as above (lock, pins, build, start)
Web --> User: 202 {name}
User -> Web: GET /api/environments/c-x7k2qa (poll)
Web -> DB: read state / pins / URLs
Web --> User: READY, https://phub-c-x7k2qa.cafitac.com
@enduml

@startuml
title Revision 4 — PR cross-link reconcile (phub-bot loop, every interval)

participant "phub-bot" as Bot
database "Registry (SQLite)" as DB
participant "GitHub API" as GH

Bot -> DB: active environments whose services use requested_ref pr-<n>\n+ pr_links rows
loop each (env, repo, pr) wanted but missing or rendered_version < env.version
  alt comment_id is null
    Bot -> GH: POST issue comment (marker <!-- phub-link env=... -->)
    Bot -> DB: txn: set comment_id, rendered_version, status ACTIVE, attempts 0
  else
    Bot -> GH: PATCH comment body
    Bot -> DB: txn: rendered_version = env.version
  end
end
loop each ACTIVE row whose environment is DELETED / gone
  Bot -> GH: PATCH comment "preview <env>: removed"
  Bot -> DB: status REMOVED
end
note right of Bot
  Failure: attempts += 1, retried next loop (no state change elsewhere).
  Crash between POST and txn: next loop searches the PR's comments
  for the marker before posting again (no duplicate).
end note
@enduml

